{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he led forth his trained men etc.</b> Abraham said to them: We are going out to war — whoever is afraid of sins in his hand, let him go and return to his house. When they heard this, they went and returned home, and there did not remain with Abraham except Eliezer his servant. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham: All of them you have dismissed — I give the strength of your life to Eliezer against all of them. And whence? The letters of אליעזר amount to the numerical value of 18 and 300. And so it is concluded in chapter 4 of Nedarim. And further it is concluded: ״וירק את חניכיו״ — Rav said that he emptied them of Torah, and Shmuel said that he emptied them of gold, meaning, so that their hearts would not be inclined otherwise but to saving lives."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:54.326897385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}